Default value: false.', example='false'),
  features?: {
    imdsSupport?: string(name='ImdsSupport', description='The metadata access mode of the image. Valid values:
- v1: When you create an ECS instance from this image, you cannot set the metadata access mode to "hardened mode only".
- v2: When you create an ECS instance from this image, you can set the metadata access mode to "hardened mode only".

Default value: v1.', example='v2'),
    nvmeSupport?: string(name='NvmeSupport', description='Specifies whether the image supports NVMe.

- supported: The image has the NVMe driver installed.
- unsupported: The image does not have the NVMe driver installed.
- If this parameter is not specified or the value is empty, the default value is unsupported.
> By default, imported images are considered as not supporting the NVMe protocol. If you plan to run the image on instance types that support NVMe (such as c8i and r9i), make sure that the image has a built-in NVMe driver and explicitly set this parameter to supported.', example='supported'),
  }(name='Features', description='The image feature-related properties.'),
  imageName?: string(name='ImageName', description='The image name. The name must be 2 to 128 characters in length. It must start with a letter or a Chinese character and cannot start with `aliyun` or `acs:`. It cannot contain `http://` or `https://`. It can contain digits, periods (.), colons (:), underscores (_), or hyphens (-).', example='ImageTestName'),
  licenseType?: string(name='LicenseType', description='The license type. This parameter specifies the authorization mode when instances are created by calling [RunInstances](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679677.html) with this image. This value takes effect only for Windows Server images. Valid values:
- Aliyun: Uses the Alibaba Cloud official license. After the instance starts, the system attempts to automatically connect to the Alibaba Cloud KMS server for activation. The billing for the instance includes the Windows Server license fee.
- BYOL: Bring Your Own License. After the instance starts, Alibaba Cloud does not automatically activate it. You must manually activate it by using your own valid license key. The billing for the instance does not include the Windows Server license fee.

Default value: Aliyun.', example='BYOL'),
  OSType?: string(name='OSType', description='The operating system type. Valid values: 

- windows. You must also set `LicenseType`.
- linux.

Default value: linux.', example='linux'),
  ownerId?: long(name='OwnerId'),
  platform?: string(name='Platform', description='The operating system distribution. Valid values: 
- Aliyun
- Anolis
- CentOS
- Ubuntu
- CoreOS
- SUSE
- Debian
- OpenSUSE
- FreeBSD
- RedHat
- Kylin
- UOS
- Fedora
- Fedora CoreOS
- CentOS Stream
- AlmaLinux
- Rocky Linux
- Gentoo
- Customized Linux
- Others Linux
- Windows Server 2022
- Windows Server 2019
- Windows Server 2016
- Windows Server 2012
- Windows Server 2008
- Windows Server 2003
- Other Windows

Default value: Others Linux.', example='Aliyun'),
  regionId?: string(name='RegionId', description='The region ID of the source custom image. You can call [DescribeRegions](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25609.html) to query the most recent region list.

This parameter is required.', example='cn-hangzhou'),
  resourceGroupId?: string(name='ResourceGroupId', description='The ID of the enterprise resource group to which the imported image belongs.', example='rg-bp67acfmxazb4p****'),
  resourceOwnerAccount?: string(name='ResourceOwnerAccount'),
  resourceOwnerId?: long(name='ResourceOwnerId'),
  roleName?: string(name='RoleName', description='The name of the RAM role used to import the image.', example='AliyunECSImageImportDefaultRole'),
  storageLocationArn?: string(name='StorageLocationArn', description='The Alibaba Cloud Resource Name (ARN) of the CloudBox, which uniquely identifies the cloud storage location.

>You need to specify this parameter only when you import an image file from OSS on CloudBox. If you are not using OSS on CloudBox, do not set this parameter. For more information, see [What is OSS on CloudBox](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/430190.html).

The correct ARN format is: `arn:acs:cloudbox:{RegionId}:{AliUid}:cloudbox/{CloudBoxId}`, where `{RegionId}` is the region ID where the CloudBox resides, `{AliUid}` is the Alibaba Cloud account ID, and `{CloudBoxId}` is the CloudBox ID.', example='arn:acs:cloudbox:cn-hangzhou:123456:cloudbox/cb-xx***123'),
